# Build context for the root Dockerfile (the all-in-one image). The context is
# the whole repository here, unlike backend/ or ui/ for the split images, so this
# file is what keeps it from including several hundred megabytes of things the
# image must not contain.

# Dependency trees -- reinstalled inside the image, and platform-specific:
# a Windows-built .venv or node_modules is not merely wasteful here, it is wrong.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Local build output. The image builds the frontend itself.
ui/dist

# Secrets. Never in an image layer, where they survive even if a later layer
# deletes them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.production.example
infra/deploy.env

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Editor/assistant working directories
.claude
.kiro
skills

# Test and tooling artifacts
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
backend/tests
backend/conftest.py
backend/pytest.ini
backend/requirements-dev.txt

# Demo-only data and the seed script: deliberately not shipped, matching
# backend/Dockerfile (see backend/specs.md Phase 5). A deployment loads real
# data through the app's CSV import instead.
backend/data
backend/scripts
statement.csv
test_statement.csv

# Deployment topologies and docs -- not needed at runtime
docs
infra
*.md
docker-compose.yml
